meta {
  name: callbacks
  seq: 8
}

docs {
  Gateway callbacks (M2 step 2) and the callback log.

  The gateway sends a callback to `{bridgeUrl}<path>`. The bridge URL is
  `${ABDM_CALLBACK_BASE_URL}/api/abdm` (ADR-005). The requests below use `careUrl`,
  so that you can probe the receiver on a local machine.

  The receiver stores every callback before it checks the signature. It then
  verifies the `Authorization` JWT against the gateway JWKS. A signature that fails
  gives HTTP 401. A signature that passes gives HTTP 202 and a Celery job.
  A repeat of the same callback gives the first result again.

  Set `callbackToken` to a signed gateway JWT. A made-up value gives HTTP 401.
  That result is correct: the receiver fails closed.

  The list and the detail routes need a superuser.
}
